# `rebuild` builds its block anew for each value of its dynamic (Semantics ch. 4), and
# `@ v` lifts a value into the widget being built: a plain function builds nothing, so a
# `rebuild` is a blueprint there, `@$Nat`, as a building `if` is (`@t`), and not the
# dynamic the signature names. prismc's back end refuses it today ("a `rebuild` outside a
# widget block as a value"); the checker should, as a mismatch.
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

$Twice: fn $Nat -> $Nat
fn $Twice $n = rebuild $n: @ _ * 2

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{$Twice ($ 1)}")
